      "thinking": "Let me analyze this fragment. It's page 5 of 5 of a certificate:\n\n- Number: R137/2012-B-NL1-18.05\n- Project number: 1901860\n- Page 5 of 5\n- Member State: The Netherlands\n- Issuing authority: NMi (Netherlands)\n\nContent:\n- Interchangeable components: mechanical index with reed contact, Wiegand or encoder\n- Installation conditions: FMT-L meter with two different flow straighteners; large straightener → 1xDN straight inlet pipe; small → 5xDN. FMT-S only with large straightener, needs minimum 1xDN. FMT-Lx no installation requirements. FMT-Dc consists of two FMT-Lx cartridges in one housing, same installation conditions as FMT-Lx.\n\nThis fragment contains:\n- certificate: number, project_number, page_total (5), member_state (The Netherlands), scheme (B from the number R137/2012-B-NL1-18.05)\n- The scheme letter B appears in the number.\n\nWhat else? The installation conditions could be captured as config_level characteristics:\n- straight_inlet_pipe_length for FMT-L with large straightener: 1xDN\n- straight_inlet_pipe_length for FMT-L with small straightener: 5xDN\n- FMT-S: 1xDN minimum\n- FMT-Lx: none required\n- FMT-Dc: same as FMT-Lx (no requirements)\n\nAlso components: mechanical index (interchangeable component) with variants reed contact OR Wiegand OR encoder — alternatives \"OR\".\n\nThe DN value isn't given numerically; it's a formula-like value \"1xDN\" or \"5xDN\". Keep as strings.\n\nConfig_level entries:\n- attribute: straight_inlet_pipe_length, axis: flow_straightener / meter_model\n- Values:\n  - condition: \"FMT-L with large flow straightener\", value: \"1xDN\"\n  - condition: \"FMT-L with small flow straightener\", value: \"5xDN\"\n  - condition: \"FMT-S\", value: \"minimum 1xDN\" — but value should keep numeric separate... These are formulas \"1 x DN\", keep as strings with unit_symbol maybe \"×DN\" or just string. I'd use value as string \"1 x DN\", unit_symbol null. Actually could represent as {value: 1, unit_symbol: \"×DN