odels\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-L\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-S\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-Lx\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FMT-Dc\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"interchangeable_component\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"mechanical index with reed contact\", \"mechanical index with Wiegand\", \"mechanical index with encoder\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n      \"characteristics\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"flow_straightener\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"large flow straightener\", \"small flow straightener\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n      \"characteristics\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"straight_inlet_pipe_length\",\n        \"axis\": \"meter model and flow straightener\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with large flow straightener\", \"value\": \"1 x DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with small flow straightener\", \"value\": \"5 x DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-S (large flow straightener only)\", \"value\": \"minimum 1 x DN\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-Lx (flow straightener installed)\", \"value\": \"no requirement\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"FMT-Dc (two FMT-Lx cartridges in one housing)\", \"value\": \"same as FMT-Lx\"}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nFamily name \"FMT\" — is it explicit? Models FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx, FMT-Dc share prefix FMT. It's implicit; the rules say explicit family name if any, else null. Not explicitly stated; set null.\n\nShould the \"value\" for conditions be structured objects? Rule 5: \"Values follow the same structured form: {condition, value, unit_symbol}.\" So value can be string for formulas. Good.\n\nThe components rule 6 says record each with role, type_designations, sub-characteristics; alternatives \"OR\". The mechanical index variants: \"equipped with a reed contact, Wiegand or encoder\" — that's about the index's pulse pickup, alternatives OR. Fine.\n\nShould flow straighteners be components? They are equipment the meter can be equipped with — accessories. I'll include as components with role \"flow_straightener\". For FMT-S only large is allowed; FMT-Lx has an inlet flow straightener identical to FMT-S configuration (i.e., the large one? \"The inlet flow straightener is identical to the FMT-S configuration due to the fact that the FMT-Lx and FMT-S have identical cartridges.\" FMT-S only has the large one, so FMT-Lx's inlet straightener is the large one.) This nuance can go into characteristics:\n\nflow_straightener characteristics:\n- \"fmt_s_allowed\": \"large only\" ... maybe better as config_level. Keep simple.\n\nMaybe add characteristics in components entry:\n\"characteristics\": {\"applicability\": {\"FMT-L\": [\"large\", \"small\"], \"FMT-S\": [\"large\"], \"FMT-Lx\": [\"large\"], \"FMT-Dc\": [\"same as FMT-Lx\"]}}\n\nThat's non-standard shape. I'll keep config_level as the canonical place and keep components light.\n\nAlso, could record \"certified_type\" description mentioning FMT-Dc composition. Add certified_type with description? The fragment describes installation; description field is \"free-text description if present\". The composition \"The FMT-Dc meter consists of two FMT-Lx cartridges in one housing\" is a description element. I could include certified_type.description. Hmm — but part fragments: earlier parts presumably had the description. To be safe, I'll include a brief description of what's in the fragment? The instruction says extract content present in this fragment; the composition statement is present. I'll include a description combining composition and interchangeable components? Risk of duplication with earlier parts. I'll include certified_type.description with the FMT-Dc composition sentence since it's substantive.\n\nActually, careful: This is a fragment task; the merger presumably combines parts. Omitting certified_type is safer? But sche